      "authorImage": "https://yt3.ggpht.com/ytc/AIdro_mONpybk5BKKF6x3SzbSrhRUHhVRZvS2HdwvwaxPJoyRB8=s48-c-k-c0x00ffffff-no-rj",
      "text": "I’ve been wanting to go to Pinkerton’s but it looks way too expensive. Most BBQ (just about everyone) has ‘meat plates’. Examples would be ‘One meat’ ‘Two meat and ‘Three meat’. You choose different meats and usually get two sides. For whatever reason Pinkerton’s doesn’t offer this so if you want some brisket it’s going to cost you $35 and if you want some sides that’s gonna be extra. They also seem to charging for pickles and onions which is beyond crazy. \n\nI ate at Pizztola’s the other day. Many of the sides were subpar. The potato salad was very good though. The chicken was good but the brisket was just mediocre. I’d personally never recommend it with all the other options out there.\n\nNever heard of the brisket and rice place but I want to check it out now.",
